Subject: [PATCH 02/13] tei-v7 prompt-02: Implementation-versus-ancillary file
 filtering

---
 ExpeRepair-v1.0/agents/agent_search.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ExpeRepair-v1.0/agents/agent_search.py b/ExpeRepair-v1.0/agents/agent_search.py
index f19e7db..9c4dc6d 100644
--- a/ExpeRepair-v1.0/agents/agent_search.py
+++ b/ExpeRepair-v1.0/agents/agent_search.py
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ SELECT_FILE_PROMPT_INITIAL = """First decompose the issue into: (a) the external
 
 IMPORTANT:
 1. Select files ONLY FROM THE PROVIDED LIST and specify their FULL PATHS, starting from the root directory. Do not include any test files.
-2. If multiple files share the same name but are in different directories, and the issue description does not specify a particular one, include all relevant ones.
+2. Resolve duplicate filenames by inspecting their directory role and the issue's execution path. Prefer the file imported or called by the affected production code; exclude alternate backends, generated copies, vendored code, documentation, and unrelated tests unless repository evidence shows that the issue is implemented there. Include multiple same-named files only when the issue demonstrably affects multiple execution paths, and state the evidence for each selection.
 3. Separate each file path with a new line. Wrap the list in triple backticks (```).
 
 Explain your reasoning, then provide your answer in the following format:
